        "style": "",
        "text": "Short Description:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Requires covered public and private K-12 and postsecondary schools to classify athletic teams as male, female, or coeducational based on sex and restricts participation on sex-designated teams as specified in the measure.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Analysis and Commentary:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Oppose. Proposition 134 was placed on the ballot through a citizen initiative backed by the conservative group “",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Protect Kids Colorado",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.denverrepublicanwomen.org/post/special-guest-speaker-erin-leeexecutive-director-of-protect-kids-colorado-a-passionate-advocate-fo"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ",” founded by anti-LGBTQ+ activist ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Erin Lee",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.cpr.org/2026/04/16/colorado-mothers-pro-and-against-transgender-ballot-initiatives/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ".",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Proposition 134 follows a nationwide push by right-wing groups to criminalize, ostracize, and pretend that trans and intersex people do not exist and do not have rights to participate in society as themselves.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "So far, Colorado has avoided implementing cruel policy at the state level — while a number of states have passed policies like bathroom bans and other exclusionary measures. ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "These discriminatory endeavors are part of the broader, escalating wave of attacks on basic civil rights. These attacks include attempts to ban essential health care for transgender youth and adults, restrict participation in sports, block accurate identity documents, curb freedom of expression, endanger transgender inmates by incarcerating them in institutions inconsistent with their gender identity, and suppress and even criminalize books, education, and culture by and about LGBTQ people.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Misleading Narratives About Transgender People and Restrooms, Locker Rooms, and Other Single-Sex Spaces",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://glaad.org/fact-sheet-misleading-narratives-about-transgender-people-and-restrooms-locker-rooms-and-other-single-sex-spaces/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 8,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " — GLAAD",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Trans sports bans are no different. I have seen plenty of Republican-led efforts to promote exclusionary policy here, and some Democrats not stand up for civil rights, which erodes the rights of all of us. Trans sports bans harm all kids with exclusionary and invasive policy, and we don’t have to stand by it. If the Democratic Governor of Kentucky can take this stand, so can any Democrat:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Kentucky Governor Andy Beshear defends Democratic candidates against super PAC ads running against them on transgender issues: \"That is not the Party that we are. We start as a Party of compassion and empathy. And I tell you what, if we want to ruin sports, put the government in charge of them.\"",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Beshear reacts to transgender ads: 'Sports need to be fair, and there should be no unfair advantage.'",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.cnn.com/2026/09/27/politics/video/beshear-transgender-athletes-sotu"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 8,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " — CNN",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Lastly, I’ve seen a number of arguments that trans sports bans are about protecting women’s sports, but these arguments are disingenuous. ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "The Women’s National Basketball Association (WNBA) Minnesota Lynx coach Cheryl Reeve:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "\"I think that's probably one of the more meaningful things that would mark the season for me. It's that the transgender community is one that deserves our support and what is happening in the name of some issues of transgender in sports. It's really an attack on all transgender community, they don't want transgender people to exist.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "‘They don’t want trans people to exist’ – Lynx’s Cheryl Reeve speaks her mind",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/don-t-want-trans-people-133500831.html?guccounter=1"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 8,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " — Yahoo! Sports",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Republicans and right-wing organizations attacks on trans people more generally are hypocritically used as “protecting women,” when they do not:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "As Republicans on the Senate Judiciary Committee are expected to use today’s hearing on the Equality Act to attack trans people (and to justify their opposition to expanding anti-discrimination protections for LGBTQ people as a defense of women), a brief audit of their records reveal some of the most radical, extreme opposition to women’s equality.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "1. Not a single Republican member of the Senate cosponsored the ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Senate Athletics Fair Pay Act (2019)",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.congress.gov/bill/116th-congress/senate-bill/2083/cosponsors?searchResultViewType=expanded"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " despite talking about their support for the U.S. Women’s Soccer Team.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "2. Not a single Republican on the Senate Judiciary Committee supported the Violence Against Women Act.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "3. Republican Senators have instead taken actions to codify discrimination against women and young people.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Senate Judiciary Republicans Will Use “Women” to Justify Attacks on Trans People, But a Brief Review of GOP’s Radical Opposition to Women’s Equality Reveals their Real Motivations and Hypocrisy",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.hrc.org/press-releases/senate-judiciary-republicans-will-use-women-to-justify-attacks-on-trans-people-but-a-brief-review-of-gops-radical-opposition-to-womens-equality-reveals-their-real-motivations-and-hypocrisy"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 8,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " — Human Rights Campaign",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Lastly on trans participation in sports, I’ll you with this wisdom from Imani Gandy:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "type": "html",
    "version": 1,
    "html": "<blockquote class=\"bluesky-embed\" data-bluesky-uri=\"at://did:plc:fvzkql2aqtbk7qmqjkoo2lv2/app.bsky.feed.post/3mvdcuksdi22n\" data-bluesky-cid=\"bafyreickwmdqsviv3crqld4zydbaqfla2dixwwsprej4ejvwa5rcp2skem\"><p lang=\"en\">The international chess Federation banned trans women from playing women's chess.\n\nCHESS.\n\nIt's not about fairness. The fairness argument is intended to radicalize people into more violent forms of transphobia.</p>&mdash; <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:fvzkql2aqtbk7qmqjkoo2lv2?ref_src=embed\">🎃 Imani Gandy Corn 🎃 (@angryblacklady.blacksky.app)</a> <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:fvzkql2aqtbk7qmqjkoo2lv2/post/3mvdcuksdi22n?ref_src=embed\">2026-09-12T14:42:15.960Z</a></blockquote>\n<script async src=\"https://embed.bsky.app/static/embed.js\" charset=\"utf-8\"></script>",
    "visibility": {
